<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sinja</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sinja Valley</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sinja is a valley in Jumla district in the Karnali region of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a> that served as the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khasa-malla-kingdom">Khasa Malla kingdom</a> from the 12th to the 14th century. Remains of temples, stone pillars and inscriptions survive there. It is regarded as the place where the Khas language, the ancestor of modern Nepali, was first written.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sinja.jpg" alt="Sinja" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Soraj Shahi · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Narakot_Sinja_Valley.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
